cture fails in dimension nine","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/lean/docs/156.md"}},"provenance":{"kind":"computed-navigation","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","repository":"https://github.com/openai/math","rule":"Projection of the pinned ledger; no new mathematical assessment."},"reader_comparison":{"headline_coverage":"agree","method":"Compare reported scope categories; notes remain attributed and are not adjudicated.","points":[{"definitions_to_check":null,"gap":null,"note":null,"reading":"reading:6fc923254c02452a88711699","source_term":"MATCHES","state":"all"},{"definitions_to_check":null,"gap":null,"note":"`main_theorem`: the set {uu^T : ‖u‖ = 1} ⊆ `EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin 4 × Fin 4)` (Frobenius metric) is compact, lies in the trace-one symmetric matrices, has `Metric.diam = √2`, and admits no cover by ten sets of diameter < √2 (pieces taken inside the set, w.l.o.g.). The routine step not stated in Lean is that the trace-one symmetric 4×4 matrices form a 9-dimensional affine subspace (10 - 1), isometric to ℝ⁹.","reading":"reading:155eb85eb1120c8366f9a07c","source_term":"full","state":"all"}],"readings":["reading:6fc923254c02452a88711699","reading:155eb85eb1120c8366f9a07c"],"state":"agree"},"readings":[{"availability":"recorded","credit":{"atlas_pin":"8056826bbd00caea871ad036bd295182e2bef3e2","authors":[{"handle":"carlostoledo1891","name":"Carlos Toledo"}],"kind":"third-party-reported","license":"MIT","method":"Every Comparator challenge re-run on Linux with nanoda switched on, decided by a preregistered rule; every family's challenge statements read against OpenAI's headline, clause by clause. Decider: Comparator (leanprover/comparator d03acab1 = tag v4.34.0, built with the release's toolchain v4.34.1), lean4export 076e8e57, landrun 811cfff5, nanoda_lib 3a240721 — on GitHub's Linux runners (.github/workflows/openai-math-kernel.yml), one j","name":"Carlos Toledo, cert-machine","pin":"9814e4c06281e3